' STORM LIGHT
' An original game by Claude (an AI made by Anthropic) for Amy Studio,
' 2026, in Amy by Amy Bienvenu: a ray-cast lighthouse on a ColecoVision.
'
' The game: a storm night. You are the keeper of a lighthouse. Ships come
' in from the sea one after another; when one reaches the rocks, the
' beacon at the top of the tower must be lit, or she is wrecked. The
' beacon burns oil, and gusts of wind blow it out, and the wall lamps too.
' Carry oil up from the barrel in the store (your hand lantern burns it
' as well), relight what the wind put out, find the key to the storm door
' each night. Fog rolls in from the sea and shortens your view. Keep the
' light until dawn; three wrecks end the game.
'
' Controls (either joystick): up walks, down steps back, left and right
' turn. The button: the thing you face, close by (fill your lantern at
' the barrel, light a lamp or the beacon, pour oil into the beacon, take
' the key, unlock the door); facing nothing, it shutters your lantern on
' or off. Walk into stairs to climb or go down. Keypad not used.
'
' How it is drawn: NIGHT ROUNDS' ray caster (gen.py, ray_src.asm ->
' ray.asm) on 16 x 16 floors; feature faces (windows, lamps, the beacon,
' doors...) take the tiles of their current state; fog is a depth limit
' that darkens walls near it and turns farther columns into murk.

